Parity unit : page:battery/EnergyFlow   kind=page   web route=/energy-flow
Web source  : web/src/features/battery/pages/EnergyFlowPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/EnergyFlowPage/{EnergyFlowPage.Model.cs, .Source.cs, .ViewModel.cs, .cs}
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent UserControl view), exactly as the
  sibling W7 VehicleCostPage / TrueCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "EnergyFlowPage.xaml +
  EnergyFlowPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Battery" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("EnergyFlow", already in RouteTable.cs L270 →
  /energy-flow, group BatteryEnergy) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useEnergyFlow (GET /vehicles/{id}/energy/flow). The web page
  ALSO runs a second, un-named query — a raw useQuery on GET /vehicles/{id}/energy?days=N — that drives the page's
  top-level loading/empty/error state (web `isLoading = statsLoading`, `!stats`), with the real-time flow reading
  overlaid on the diagram. Both are ported: EnergyFlowClientFeed (EnergyFlowPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated
  OpenAPI contract client operations get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_energy (path vehicleID + snake_case `days`
  query, matching the web hook) and get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_energy_flow (path vehicleID). Both operation ids
  resolve against the generated endpoint table (ApiEndpoints.cs L525/L526) — asserted by
  ClientFeed_operations_resolve_against_the_generated_endpoint_table + the FakeApiClient request-shaping tests.
  The descriptors declare zero query params, so GeneratedApiClient.BuildQuery permits the trailing `days` param
  (allowed.Count==0 path). The default EnergyFlowPage() ctor uses EmptyEnergyFlowFeed (the no-data empty state),
  mirroring VehicleCostPage; the client feed is exercised by tests. No HTTP touches the view.
- The flow reading is a BEST-EFFORT overlay: the web useEnergyFlow query is retry:false, so a flow failure leaves
  the diagram on its null-safe zeros (it never errors the page). The view-model swallows flow-fetch failures and
  only the historical stats query drives the error state (test ViewModel_flow_failure_does_not_error_the_page).
- The web renders its states INSIDE the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent
  regions per ADR-006: loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton + TsChartBlockSkeleton + TsTableSkeleton shimmer; error ->
  TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry; empty -> a TsGlassPanel + TsEmptyState ("No energy flow data
  available …"); success -> the six energy sections. Never a blank region; per-chart empty bodies cover a missing
  daily breakdown (TsChartContainer.State = Empty).
- SI units (ADR-002): all DB/API/struct/TS values are SI (Wh, m, Wh/m). Conversion happens ONLY at the render
  boundary through the shared SI port — UnitFormatters.FormatEnergy (web useUnits formatEnergy, default kWh @ 2dp)
  and FormatDistance (default km @ 1dp), and NumberFormatting.Format for fmtNumber-style values (kW @ 1dp, counts @
  0dp, co2 @ 1dp). The web's manual Wh/m → Wh/km (×1000) / Wh/mi (×1609.344) efficiency math is reproduced verbatim
  in EnergyFlowProjection.EfficiencyForDisplay / EfficiencyRaw (rounded half-away-from-zero, matching JS
  toFixed/Math.round), pinned by EfficiencyForDisplay_matches_web + Metric_tiles_use_imperial_units_when_preferred.
  Calendar daily-breakdown dates are parsed AssumeLocal so a date-only "YYYY-MM-DD" renders as that calendar day in
  any runner timezone (web formatDateShort) — deterministic regardless of CI tz.
- i18n (ADR-014): this web page uses the natural-language English string as the i18next key (t('Energy Flow'),
  t('AC Power'), …) — unlike VehicleCostPage's dotted keys. All 44 manifest strings flow through ILocalizer
  .GetString("<web key>", "<English default>") in EnergyFlowProjection (resolved UNCONDITIONALLY at the top of
  Project so every key is recorded in every data state — tests Projection_resolves_every_required_string_key +
  _even_in_the_loading_state). 18 of the 44 already existed in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (single-token
  natural keys the i18n generator emits from web/src/i18n/en.json); the 26 multi-word keys are NOT present in the
  web en.json (the web relies on i18next key-fallback for them, which ILocalizer.GetString reproduces by returning
  the English fallback on a catalog miss). To satisfy the "every visible literal sourced from .resw" criterion I
  added those 26 keys verbatim (web key names, "translation.<English>") to all three catalogs in correct
  JS-ordinal sorted position (CO₂ uses U+2082 ₂, matching the web/manifest), preserving LF/UTF-8-no-BOM. NOTE: the
  resw is generator-owned and sources from web en.json; these 26 hand-added keys would not be re-emitted by
  gen-i18n until the same keys land in web en.json — documented here, not silent. The resw is not part of the
  dotnet build, so this does not affect the build gate.
- The 6 historical summary tiles use the shared TsStatCard (web StatCard/MetricCard family: accent glyph + label +
  value + unit sub-line) — its glyph carries the icon and its Sublabel carries the unit, the two content-bearing
  parts of the web MetricCard; the web's decorative per-card color is the only dropped element.
- Charts use the W3 native wrappers (never a web canvas): TsRadialGauge (SOC), TsAreaChart (daily energy),
  TsBarChart ×2 (daily distance, daily efficiency), each framed by TsChartContainer with its loading/empty/error/
  ready bodies + accessible data-view. SI values are plotted directly (web parity: energy_wh, distance_m).
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties.SetName on the page, every panel, the table, the error/empty surfaces and
  each flow node/edge/efficiency tile; the charts publish ChartAccessibility summaries + a tabular DataView.
- Build defects found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): (1) the view omitted
  `using TeslaSync.App.Core;` (StatusKind), a CS0103 that cascaded into spurious XAML-compiler WMC0001 "Unknown
  type" noise on unrelated ComponentGallery types — same false-cascade the sibling VehicleCostPage hit; fixed by
  the using. (2) The app project sets TreatWarningsAsErrors=true + AnalysisLevel=latest, so two analyzer findings
  surfaced as errors: CA1859 (SortByDateDescending returned IEnumerable → changed to concrete List<>) and CA1822
  (BuildLoadingPanel didn't touch instance state → made static). (3) Two date tests were timezone-sensitive
  (date-only parsed UTC then shown local shifted a day on the UTC-7 runner) — fixed at the source by parsing
  calendar dates AssumeLocal. All repaired; sln builds 0 Error(s), my files 0 Warning(s) (the 34 remaining warning
  lines are all pre-existing TeslaSync.App.Core CA1716/CA1859, none in this surface or the App project).

